WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.283
An internet address identifies a network endpoint for routing, but public address ownership and application control are different concepts.

00:00:09.283 --> 00:00:18.112
Registry data may associate an address range with a network operator, cloud provider, content-delivery network, or hosting company.

00:00:18.112 --> 00:00:21.509
Cloud platforms allocate and reassign addresses.

00:00:21.509 --> 00:00:26.263
Shared hosting places multiple customers on the same infrastructure.

00:00:26.263 --> 00:00:32.376
Content-delivery networks and reverse proxies present provider addresses while shielding an origin.

00:00:32.376 --> 00:00:38.036
Managed security services may also stand between users and the application.

00:00:38.036 --> 00:00:41.432
These layers make simple attribution unreliable.

00:00:41.432 --> 00:00:53.432
An address observed in DNS does not automatically identify the organization operating the application, the physical server location, or the party responsible for an event.

00:00:53.432 --> 00:00:58.639
Additional domain, certificate, provider, timing, and internal evidence is required.

00:00:58.639 --> 00:01:02.488
Geolocation databases estimate location and can disagree.

00:01:02.488 --> 00:01:11.771
They may identify a provider office, registration country, network hub, or outdated assignment rather than the system's physical position.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:18.789
Report geolocation as an estimate with source and date, not as a precise fact.

00:01:18.789 --> 00:01:22.638
Hosting context remains useful for defensive work.

00:01:22.638 --> 00:01:33.279
It can reveal external dependencies, concentration risk, provider changes, unrecognized public assets, or infrastructure that should be reconciled with contracts and inventories.

00:01:33.279 --> 00:01:38.939
Document observed addresses, source dates, provider context, shared-infrastructure limitations, and confidence.

00:01:38.939 --> 00:01:42.336
Avoid intrusive probing or access attempts.

00:01:42.336 --> 00:01:50.260
Escalate questions through authorized asset owners and vendors so public indicators are validated against operational records.
